From 384cff3185417e7838a57a26fea6543707ea8857 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Gilmore <dennis@ausil.us>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:53:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Port to modern .NET for Linux (x86_64/aarch64) and
 Windows builds

- Convert imlac.csproj to SDK-style targeting net10.0 (RollForward=Major),
  replacing the .NET Framework 4.0 / x86-only project.
- Switch to ppy.SDL2-CS (bundles native SDL2 for win-x64 and linux-x64;
  falls back to system libSDL2 elsewhere, e.g. linux-arm64) and add
  System.IO.Ports.
- HighResTimer now uses Stopwatch; FrameTimer keeps the Win32 timer queue
  on Windows and uses a Stopwatch sleep/spin scheduler elsewhere.
- Only call SetProcessDPIAware on Windows; drop unused WinForms import.
- Resolve libSDL2-2.0.so.0 on Linux when the unversioned .so is missing.
- Replace Thread.Abort (unsupported on .NET Core) with a background
  debugger thread and Environment.Exit.
- Locate boot files relative to the executable.
- Use File.ReadAllBytes for paper tapes to avoid partial reads.
- Solution uses Any CPU.
- Replace Travis/AppVeyor with a GitHub Actions matrix (linux-x64,
  linux-arm64, win-x64) publishing self-contained single-file builds.
- Document build steps and SDL2 requirements in README.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
